load @term/seed/code/structure/monoid
  find monoid

load @term/seed/code/structure/function/binary
  find binary-function

# Associative computation: computing by an associative operation, where the grouping of the work does not change the
# answer. Because a monoid's operation associates, a long fold can be reassociated into a balanced tree and evaluated in
# parallel (the parallel-prefix or scan pattern), and partial results can be combined in any order. Associativity is
# exactly what makes a computation parallelizable and order-independent. In the substrate this is why the dynamics are
# clean: the twenty-four directions compose associatively (they are the binary tetrahedral group, the unit quaternions,
# an associative rung of the tower), so reductions over the mesh are well-defined however they are grouped. The form
# carries the monoid whose associative operation the computation folds; its associativity is proved over the integers in
# the number files.
form associative-computation
  link monoid, like monoid
  link combine, like binary-function
